 "readme": "# This account\n\nThis is the search ads account for a poker training app. Its ads show to people searching for the phrases in its keyword groups, `g01` to `g40`; the platform behind the `sim` command runs them, and `sim catalog` describes what it offers.\n\n`history.csv` holds what ran before on this account.\n\nTicks run for you every 12 hours.\n\nTo reach me, run `notify`; `notify --help` says how it works.\n\nThis account has no Google access; keep the hill climb's workbook as CSV files in `workbook/`.\n\nReports for me go in `reports/` as HTML or Markdown files.\n",
 "setup_prompt": "/hill-climb Set up a hill climb on these search keywords to get the cost of a conversion as low as possible. You have $400; ask me if you need more."
